course: dictionary
lesson: 523
title: Asthma: when breathing is hard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Asthma is an illness that makes the small air tubes in the lungs become narrow. Air has a harder time going in and out, so breathing feels hard. «In an asthma attack, sit the person up, help them use their reliever inhaler and fetch an adult.» The words around asthma tell you it is serious and that people need help.
explain: The clues in a text show what asthma feels like. A person may cough, wheeze or feel a tight chest. Wheeze is a whistling sound made when air squeezes through narrow tubes.
explain: «Colds often trigger asthma.» A trigger is something that sets off a problem. Other triggers include exercise, cold air, dust, pollen and smoke. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then check your meaning fits.
fact: Asthma is an illness that makes the small air tubes in the lungs become narrow.
fact: People with asthma may cough, wheeze and feel a tight chest.
fact: A trigger is something that can set off asthma, such as dust, pollen, smoke, cold air or exercise.
fact: An inhaler, sometimes called a puffer, gives medicine that helps open the airways.
fact: You say «have asthma», not «have an asthma», because asthma is uncountable.
exercise: «Colds often trigger asthma, so a child with asthma keeps the reliever inhaler close.» What is an inhaler? | *A puffer with medicine that helps open the airways | A kind of cold drink | A type of bandage | A small tent for camping
exercise: Which of these can trigger asthma? | Reading a book | *Dust | Drinking a glass of water | A good night's sleep
exercise: «In an asthma attack, sit the person up, help them use their reliever inhaler and fetch an adult.» What should you do if a friend has an asthma attack? | Give them a sweet drink and run away | Tell them to hold their breath | Leave them alone to rest | *Sit them up, help them use their inhaler and fetch an adult
test: Which is the best meaning of asthma? | Narrow air tubes in the lungs make breathing hard | *An illness that narrows the small air tubes in the lungs, so breathing is hard | A kind of sweet food that children eat | A sore toe after running
test: Which sentence uses asthma correctly? | She has the asthmas. | She has an asthmas. | *She has asthma.
exam: Which is a sign of asthma? | Growing ten centimetres in one day | Glowing skin | *Wheezing and a tight chest | A sore toe
